 "declarations": [
  "Secondary analysis only: our probabilities are the frozen holdout predictions, evaluated on a subset of rows and/or against a swapped label; no new forward pass, once-only protocol intact.",
  "Every number inside one figure uses one row set, one label, one window and one metric recipe; model input/training differences are the object of comparison.",
  "Figure A is a 3-way-intersection subset of the official 3,004-row test table; the official headline numbers are unchanged and remain in the main table.",
  "Figure B thresholds are re-derived under CMA-25.27kt on val 2018-19 rows; the USA-30kt 0.225 threshold is not transplanted.",
  "CVRI-Ens and the statistical baselines are evaluated across label sources in figure B: USA-30kt fit-period labels (2000-2017), inner-period labels (2018-2019), and CMA-25.27kt evaluation labels (2020-2021). RITCF uses CMA labels and is evaluated across label sources in figure A.",
  "WRPS1's final coefficients and probability mapping were fitted on 2002-2021, overlapping figure B's two evaluation years and two years of figure A and the 2,892-row comparison.",
  "RITCF variant V1 uses a rolling reference pool that admits within-test-year labels; this is the model's own protocol, carried here unchanged and flagged wherever V1 is read.",
  "The paper claim (POD 91.0 / FARate 9.4 / FARatio 58.7, n=1,149) appears as an open external anchor only: different sample, different label pipeline, different evaluation code; it is not connected to any curve.",
  "Figure B has only 66 RI rows: the binomial s.d. of POD is about 6 points at POD 0.5 (95% +-12 points), so smaller differences are not resolvable and no significance is claimed for them.",
  "BSS uses the fixed development-period climatology 0.0791 as the reference rate."
 ],
